     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first, because as written it's well above the maximum.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Per dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Per day:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6400 mg/day**. The usual adult maximum is **3200 mg/day**, so this is double that.\n\nDoses this high carry a real risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and other toxicity, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **Ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth, four times daily.** That's 1600 mg per day in total, so 1600 mg may have been meant as the daily total.\n2. **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, three times daily.** That's 2400 mg per day.\n3. **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, four times daily.** That's 3200 mg per day, the maximum.\n4. Something else.\n\nTell me which one, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do mean 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical reason, and I'll add it to the order note. Even then, I'd recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
