     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered this order. You've confirmed the dose, but without a clinical reason I can't put through an order at double the maximum daily dose.\n\nAt 6400 mg/day, ibuprofen is a toxic dose with no standard adult indication. The main risks are GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis and CNS effects. A healthy kidney and liver don't make this dose safe. (High-dose ibuprofen in cystic fibrosis is weight-based and given twice daily, not four times, and needs drug-level monitoring.)\n\n**To move forward, either:**\n- **Give me the indication or protocol** (for example a research protocol, or a level-guided regimen with monitoring). I'll enter the order as written with that reason and an over-maximum warning in the order note, so pharmacy can verify it.\n- **Or pick a standard dose,** such as 400 mg or 800 mg by mouth four times daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n\nIf this is meant for an unusual situation, I'd strongly recommend talking to the clinical pharmacist before giving the first dose."
      }
     ],
